   28. THE STACK — a hi-fi component rack, in a window
   --------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Three units bolted into one rail: a disc transport on top, an amplifier
   with its equaliser in the middle, and an analyser across the bottom. The
   whole face is drawn into one small canvas and blown up with nearest
   neighbour, so the knobs have jagged edges and the meters step — rack gear
   photographed badly, not a web page.

   None of it is decorative. The knobs are BiquadFilterNodes, the meters read
   an AnalyserNode, the room is a ConvolverNode with an impulse we synthesise
   at start-up, and the bundled records are rendered to AudioBuffers by an
   OfflineAudioContext so a built-in track and a file you dropped in are the
   same kind of thing from the moment they hit the playlist.
